EDICT 0001: COM_FileBase read before the start of its argument

Category: undefined behaviour, no change in results.
The loop that searches backwards for '/' stopped only at '/' or a zero byte, so for paths without '/'
(first hit: "gfx.wad" from W_LoadWadFile in Host_Init) it read the bytes in front of the string. The
1996 32-bit builds happened to find a zero byte there; the x64 clang build does not and crashes
(AddressSanitizer: global-buffer-overflow in COM_FileBase). The rewrite stops at the start of the
string and returns what the original returned with a zero byte in front: checked on 21 edge-case
paths, 0 differences (see the commit that adds this patch).

--- a/common.c
+++ b/common.c
@@ -855,23 +855,24 @@
 */
 void COM_FileBase (char *in, char *out)
 {
-	char *s, *s2;
+	char *s, *b;
 	
 	s = in + strlen(in) - 1;
 	
 	while (s != in && *s != '.')
 		s--;
 	
-	for (s2 = s ; *s2 && *s2 != '/' ; s2--)
+	// EDICT: the original loop ran before the start of 'in' when it held no '/' (e.g. "gfx.wad") and relied
+	// on a zero byte in front of the string. Same results, computed from the start of the base name.
+	for (b = s ; b != in && b[-1] != '/' ; b--)
 	;
 	
-	if (s-s2 < 2)
+	if (s-b < 1)
 		strcpy (out,"?model?");
 	else
 	{
-		s--;
-		strncpy (out,s2+1, s-s2);
-		out[s-s2] = 0;
+		strncpy (out,b, s-b);
+		out[s-b] = 0;
 	}
 }
 
